WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.584
Two changes.

00:00:01.624 --> 00:00:03.619
Each valid on its own.

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:06.817
Together, 140 against a bound of 130.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.437
Rewind.

00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:11.898
Locking the same target
serializes correctly.

00:00:11.938 --> 00:00:14.813
Two different targets, two
different locks - both correct,

00:00:14.853 --> 00:00:17.048
and the hazard spans them.

00:00:17.088 --> 00:00:21.778
The bound is a property of the environment;
no per-key lock takes it as input.

00:00:21.818 --> 00:00:24.920
The hazard lives in the
relationship between the files,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.835
and that relationship is
in the repository history.

00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:30.750
Interlock reads it before
the mutation, and withholds.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.706
Remove the evidence, and
the invalid result returns.

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:40.117
A global lock stays safe
by serializing everything.

00:00:40.157 --> 00:00:44.077
A credible per-target lock preserves
concurrency, but still misses both hazards,

00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:46.409
because they span different targets.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.692
Interlock uses composition evidence instead:

00:00:51.732 --> 00:00:54.953
it withheld both hazardous pairs while
keeping both independent pairs parallel.

00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:58.017
Then we removed the coupling
signal from the frozen evidence.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:01.278
Same actions, same core - the decision
flipped, and both invariants failed.

00:01:01.318 --> 00:01:03.400
The evidence is load-bearing.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.391
That was controlled evaluation.

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:07.724
What follows is a separate deployed run.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:13.682
The deployed Cloud Run agent reads
back its own configuration: gemini-3.

00:01:13.722 --> 00:01:17.096
5-flash, through Google ADK 1.

00:01:17.136 --> 00:01:18.485
35.

00:01:18.525 --> 00:01:23.965
1 with Vertex AI access, from an image
pinned to the runtime source commit.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:31.121
Three Cloud Run services carried the
run in us-central1: the ADK agent,

00:01:31.161 --> 00:01:35.150
the Interlock MCP proxy,
and the protected target.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.996
The traversal executed while
this frame was captured.

00:01:40.036 --> 00:01:44.525
Interlock returned ALLOW with a receipt
digest under one correlation id.

00:01:44.565 --> 00:01:50.197
Three fail-closed controls on the same run:
a forged identity header returned 403,

00:01:50.237 --> 00:01:55.909
an invalid bearer token 401, a
direct call with no receipt, 403.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.969
The protected mutation is
EXECUTED against that receipt.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:06.909
The resulting invariant on the target
is 105 against a bound of 130.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.080
EXECUTED is not OBSERVED.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.833
A separately authenticated,

00:02:13.873 --> 00:02:17.762
keyless observer service account read the
target back at the post-mutation revision

00:02:17.802 --> 00:02:20.167
and observed alpha at 45.

00:02:20.207 --> 00:02:23.483
Two records, not one: the model's
own output declares nothing.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.740
Cloud Logging, filtered to that same
correlation id: the proxy request,

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.860
the agent identity as
the platform verified it,

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.020
and the Cloud Run revision that served it.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:37.895
Where Interlock sits.

00:02:37.935 --> 00:02:41.737
The agent calls a tool through
the Interlock MCP proxy.

00:02:41.777 --> 00:02:45.349
Interlock reads revision-bound composition
evidence before the mutation and returns

00:02:45.389 --> 00:02:47.631
a decision with a receipt.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.793
Cloud Run IAM establishes
transport provenance.

00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:55.236
It does not establish application-role
semantics inside Interlock.

00:02:55.276 --> 00:02:59.761
Agent Runtime, Agent Gateway and
CONTENT_AUTHZ were not on this path.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.476
Two runs, two proof classes;
neither is evidence for the other.

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:07.839
Sixteen frozen scenarios, exhaustively
enumerated - exact counts, not estimates.

00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:11.454
No exactly-once execution, no restart
safety, no production readiness.

00:03:11.494 --> 00:03:14.354
ALLOW is a decision, not a verification.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.580
In this controlled corpus,

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.639
per-target locking correctly
coordinated what its keys represented,

00:03:20.679 --> 00:03:23.044
but missed hazards spanning distinct keys.

00:03:23.084 --> 00:03:26.103
With qualifying repository evidence present,
Interlock changed that coordination;

00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:28.983
when the evidence was removed,
the failures returned.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.124
Interlock makes that evidence part of the
coordination decision before shared state

00:03:34.164 --> 00:03:35.465
changes.
